  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200B;&#x200B;Addressing the Needs of Vulnerable Migrants within the Humanitarian, Development and Peace Nexus in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration plays a critical role in the growth and development of Thailand. Migrant workers are a crucial component to local and multi-national businesses operating in the country with majority of the migrant labour force coming from Myanmar. Myanmar nationals in Thailand are in a heightened situation of vulnerability as returning to their home country is often not an option for them. At the same time, Thailand is re-opening its borders and businesses are slowly increasing operations as they begin to recover from the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic. Mindful of these complex humanitarian and development challenges, this project works within the Humanitarian, Development and Peace Nexus (HDPN) and applies a rights-based and human security approach to identify and address the cross-cutting challenges they face so that urgent humanitarian needs are met while at the same time contributing to the localization of the Sustainable Development Goals in Thailand.  Ultimately, this project aims to promote equitable and inclusive societies where migrants, mobile populations (particularly Myanmar nationals) and communities are able to access essential services and have decent work. This is achieved through data collection activities, the provision of multi-sectoral assistance, as well as capacity building interventions targeting Japanese businesses.</narrative>
  </description>
